diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index ea1a1a0..d98488d 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,27 @@ Semantic Versioning.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- **Breaking**: `v1.Files.Add` now takes a file name and a content reader
+  (`Add(ctx, fileName, content, opts...)`) and builds the multipart/form-data
+  body itself, mirroring `v1.CallLogs.AddRecording`. New options
+  `WithFileActivityID`, `WithFileDealID`, `WithFileLeadID`,
+  `WithFileOrganizationID`, `WithFilePersonID`, `WithFileProductID` and
+  `WithFileProjectID` associate the upload with an item. Previously callers
+  built the multipart body themselves and passed it as a reader; such bodies
+  are not replayable, so uploads were never retried on 429/502/503/504 even
+  with `RetryAllMethods` enabled. Uploads are now buffered in memory and
+  retried like every other call; use `Raw().Do` to send a hand-built body.
+- **Breaking**: `v1.Files.Update` now takes options instead of a raw body
+  (`Update(ctx, id, WithFileName(...), WithFileDescription(...))`), matching
+  the API, which only accepts a form-encoded name and description. The
+  request body is replayable, so updates are retried too.
+- **Breaking**: `v1.Persons.AddPicture` now takes a file name and a content
+  reader (`AddPicture(ctx, id, fileName, content, opts...)`) and builds the
+  multipart body itself; `WithPersonPictureCrop` supplies optional crop
+  coordinates. The upload is buffered and retried on 429/502/503/504.
+
 ## [1.11.0] - 2026-08-18
 
 ### Added
